MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The E-clips and self-drilling screws fit my repeated interest in practical fastener assortments: they give me useful options for mechanical repairs and sheet-metal assembly alongside my cotter pins, rivets, and drill bits.",
    "The rubber grommets and wire brushes complement work I already have supplies for, by protecting wiring through drilled panels and preparing metal surfaces before further work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The calibration weights and clamp meter serve specific measurement tasks that my recent activity does not give me a reason to tackle now; owning a caliper or inspection camera does not mean I need every diagnostic tool.",
    "The vacuum chamber connects to my older resin purchase, but I have no current vacuum-processing project. The cable, quick links, and adhesive three-pack likewise need a specific job before they become useful choices for me."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat general workshop usefulness as enough, even when an item does not support the fastening, drilling, or metal preparation I am currently interested in.",
    "A past purchase seems to carry too far into specialized equipment or bulk supplies without a clear reason I would need that next step."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, rivet nuts, bolts, and retaining hardware make complementary fastening and repair supplies more relevant than loosely related workshop equipment.",
    "The actual job matters more than shared wording: rubber wiring grommets offer a different useful function from eyelet grommets, while more screws are appealing only to the extent that they add capabilities beyond my existing assortment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my hands-on repair interests but sometimes mistake broad workshop relevance for a concrete next need."
}
